Ladybird keeps an extension’s menu items for as long as it stays loaded,
and drops them when it’s reloaded, disabled, or removed, as Chromium’s
MenuManager::OnExtensionUnloaded() and Gecko’s ext-menus.js onShutdown()
do; a background page that only idles out keeps them. The errors
(“Cannot create item with duplicate id x” and “Cannot find menu item
with id x”) keep Chromium’s wording from its context_menu_helpers.cc.

commands.getAll() reports each command’s suggested key for this
platform, or its default one, with its spaces removed, as Gecko’s
ExtensionShortcuts normalizeShortcut() does; Chromium on macOS shows
the shortcut as symbols instead. An unknown command fails with Gecko’s
“Unknown command ”“x” wording.
